  "query_preview": "..\nShower coverage finally began to increase across the Marianas this\nafternoon, with numerous heavy showers seen across Guam and scattered\nshowers elsewhere earlier this afternoon. POPs (Probability of \nPrecipitation) around on the low-end, around 30 percent, for the CNMI\nand around 50 percent for Guam, which looks to be the rule through \nthe rest of the night. Latest guidance tries to bring in numerous \nshowers for the next couple of days for Guam, with very dry \nconditions across the CNMI. However, decided to maintain POPs at 30 \nto 50 percent for Guam due to this increase in convection being \nlinked to the development of a weak monsoon disturbance both \nsoutheast and southwest of Guam over the next few days. It appears \nthat development, if it occurs, will be a bit farther away from Guam,\nheading almost due north, keeping the heavier showers and higher \nPOPs away from the Marianas. Therefore, Guam looks to maintain \nscattered showers and isolated thunderstorms for the next few days, \nwith the CNMI seeing only isolated showers by Monday morning.",
